\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa120\itap0 {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://4665/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs22\chcbpat17 61ra-62va}}\plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs22  Naturphilosophisch-medizinischer {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6922/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs22\chcbpat17 Traktat}}\plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs22  (?) 
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa120\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 Abschnitte: (61ra){\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22\chcbpat17  Nota quod generacioni simplici mixti, in quantum mixtum est}}\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 , opponitur putrefactio, quia generacioni mixti opponitur corrupcio \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 ...; \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 Item nota, quod corrupcio per marcedinem\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 et per extinctionem, de quibus loquitur philosophus libro De morte et vita\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  ...; \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 Digestio est perfectio a naturali et proprio calido ex oppositis passivis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  ...; \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 Finis digestionis dicendum est vnus est intrinsecus et iste est aliqua forma \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 ...; (61rb) {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[1].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22\chcbpat17 Qualiter autem pepansis dicitur, quando calidum alterans et digerens}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  ...; \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 Epsesis est alia species digestionis, et est epsesis proprie dicta digestio a caliditate humida\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  ...; (61vb) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 Optesis est digestio facta a caliditate sicca ...\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 ; \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 Nota quod humidum et siccum sunt qualitates passive\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  ...; (62rb) {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[2].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22\chcbpat17 De differentia ingrossationis et coagulationis nota quod illa, que sunt mixta}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  ...; \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 Ex predictis possumus scire e contrario, que sint aque vel terre \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 ...; \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 Continget autem aliqua esse insolubilia sicut lapides et lateres \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 \endash  ... \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 (62va) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 in quibus sunt pori non propio reservati humido, quod ingredi possit sicut in latere.
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa120\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 Nicht identifiziert. Geschrieben (und verfasst?) von H3/NH1. Behandelt werden generatio und corruptio, verschiedene Formen der digestio (aristotelische Begriffe), coagulatio und ingrossatio. }

